          },
          {
            "source_id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:document:8e2a86970dc06b1340952160d3f6524db8f2948b72a87253bc35cda27b0de7e1",
            "quote": "( 1 ) Seats manufactured to U.S. standards between January 1, 1981, and February 25, 1985, must bear the label: “This child restraint system conforms to all applicable Federal motor vehicle safety standards”;",
            "start": 2559,
            "end": 2767
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "Claim C0007 correctly captures the mandatory requirement from paragraph (a)(3)(iii)(B)(1) that seats manufactured to U.S. standards between January 1, 1981, and February 25, 1985, must bear the specified label. However, the governing condition in the parent lead-in (B)—specifically the exception 'Except as provided in paragraph (a)(3)(iii)(B)( 4 ) of this action'—was omitted from both the summary and the explicit scope_text ('Approved child restraint systems manufactured to U.S. standards between January 1, 1981, and February 25, 1985'), despite being quoted in the raw scope_quotes. Because this governing exception was not incorporated into the explicit meaning or scope, the summary and scope are incomplete and overbroad.",
